      "en": "$tinta_higher_thres"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "The income threshold, equal to 100% of the minimum monthly wage ($MMS), from which the higher basic PIT allowance starts being withdrawn, per its label and the raw formula '100%*$MMS'. It is used in tin_admn_lt (BenCalc, parameter withdraw_start, post-2022 formula) and in tin_lt (BenCalc, parameter withdraw_start, for the final tax liability calculation since 2009), setting the income point at which allowance taper begins. Not covered by the benefits theme document; description based on the constant's own formula-stating label and usage comments."
    },
